<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 212 0 R
/E (This sequence is an ideal introductory activity to the "Robots Meet Arts" universe \(Robots and Humanities Encounter\). It allows for demystifying robotics programming in a fun way, showing that programming a robot is not reserved for experts: it is accessible, creative, and deeply connected to what we are as human beings.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
391 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 212 0 R
/E (The starting point: Imagine a robot born yesterday that must learn to navigate an unknown environment to reach a goal. Nobody has given it a map: it must discover for itself which paths are safe and which are blocked by obstacles. How can it learn without getting permanently lost?)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
