417 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 213 0 R
/E (This activity was designed as an accessible gateway to robotics programming. By starting with an "unplugged" phase where pupils are themselves the robot, we remove apprehensions: programming is simply giving clear instructions, like those they followed during the game. The transition to real robots then becomes natural and non-intimidating.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
418 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 213 0 R
/E (Three robots are proposed \(Cubetto, Sphero Indi, micro:bit\), each with a different programming logic. Ideally, all three should be discovered through rotating workshops, but the activity works very well with a single robot depending on your resources. The essential thing is to experience giving instructions to a machine and seeing your creation come to life.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
